# Takeout bag (issues 154, 157): a paper bag seen from behind and above like the other south-wall pieces, closed. The top is folded over and pinched (a white fold with a crinkled taupe edge), a twine handle loop stands up out of it, and the body shows only as a thin cream slice at the bottom with a tan side. No print, no logo, no text. 1x1 tile; sits on the floor in front of the front door, in place of the package box, only while a takeout meal waits and no package does.
size: 16x16
